 ## Overview
-The Capsule Signed Distance Function (SDF) computes the exact Euclidean distance from a query point in 3D space to the surface of a capsule, defined as a line segment (the axis) with a constant radius. It solves the problem of representing smooth, rounded tubular geometry for ray marching and volume rendering without polygonal approximation. It is distinguished from the [Sphere SDF](1237-sphere-signed-distance-function.md) by its linear axis and from the [Box SDF](1092-signed-box-distance-function.md) by its cylindrical symmetry and hemispherical ends.
+The Capsule Signed Distance Function computes the exact Euclidean distance from a query point in 3D space to the surface of a capsule, defined as a line segment with a constant radius [S3, unofficial]. It represents smooth, rounded tubular geometry for ray marching and volume rendering without polygonal approximation [G]. It is distinguished from the [Sphere SDF](1237-sphere-signed-distance-function.md) by its linear axis and from the [Box SDF](1092-signed-box-distance-function.md) by its cylindrical symmetry and hemispherical ends [G].
 
 ## How it works
